      "properties": {
        "text": ""
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Z-Image LoRA training (experimental, transformer-only by default).\n\nmodel_path accepts a local diffusers-format directory (transformer/ text_encoder/ vae/ tokenizer/ subfolders) or a HF hub repo id, e.g. Tongyi-MAI/Z-Image-Turbo.\n\nThis pipeline loads models via diffusers directly (not Kohya's own model classes like the Flux/SD3 trainers), since Kohya's sd-scripts has no Z-Image support at all.\n\nMemory: leave fp8_base OFF -- it breaks Z-Image's diffusers forward pass. Use cache_text_encoder_outputs + gradient_checkpointing instead; validated at ~14GB VRAM for a single 512x512 image on an RTX 4090.\n\nSample-image generation during training is not implemented yet -- ZImageTrainLoop only reports loss, it won't produce preview images.\n\nSet train_text_encoder to 'qwen3' to also train the Qwen3 text encoder as LoRA (must disable cache_text_encoder_outputs if you do)."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
